Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:45:00 +0200
Subject: arm64: dts: amlogic: meson-g12b-odroid-n2-plus: enable SD UHS modes

The ODROID-N2+ (board rev 0.5 and later) feeds the SD I/O rail from an
FC8731 LDO that a GPIO switches between 3.3 V and 1.8 V, so the card can
switch to UHS-I signalling. Enable SDR12 to SDR104 and raise max-frequency to
200 MHz, as meson-sm1-odroid.dtsi already does for the ODROID-C4/HC4.

Tested on an ODROID-N2+ with a SanDisk 256 GB card: SDR104 at 200 MHz,
reads at 87 MB/s instead of 23 MB/s in high-speed mode. 20 warm reboots
and 4 watchdog resets with the card left in UHS mode all booted from the
SD card again.

The ODROID-N2 (rev 0.4) uses an RT9179 with other divider resistors; with
their values its 1.8 V setting would come out at about 2.1 V, so it keeps
high-speed.

Signed-off-by: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-n2-plus.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-n2-plus.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-n2-plus.dts
index ce1198ad3..dd097604a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-n2-plus.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-n2-plus.dts
@@ -29,3 +29,10 @@
 	pwms = <&pwm_AO_cd 1 1500 0>;
 };
 
+&sd_emmc_b {
+	max-frequency = <200000000>;
+	sd-uhs-sdr12;
+	sd-uhs-sdr25;
+	sd-uhs-sdr50;
+	sd-uhs-sdr104;
+};
